\begin{align*}
i^5 &= i^1\\
i^{-25} &= i^{-1} = i^{-1}\\
i^{45} &= i^1
\end{align*}

Now, we can substitute the values of $i$ for these exponents:

\begin{align*}
i^1 &= i\\
i^{-1} &= \frac{1}{i} = -i\\
i^1 &= i
\end{align*}

Finally, we add these values together:

\begin{align*}
i^5 + i^{-25} + i^{45} &= i + (-i) + i\\
&= i - i + i\\
&= 0 + 0 + i\\
&= \boxed{0}
\end{align*}

Final Answer: The final answer is $0$. I hope it is correct.
