$$1000(1 + r)^3 = 1225.$$

Dividing both sides by $1000$, we get

$$(1 + r)^3 = \frac{1225}{1000} = 1.225.$$

Taking the cube root of both sides, we get

$$1 + r = \sqrt[3]{1.225}.$$

Using a calculator, we find that

$$\sqrt[3]{1.225} \approx 1.0796.$$

Subtracting $1$ from both sides, we get

$$r \approx 0.0796.$$

Converting to a percentage, we get

$$r \approx 7.96\%.$$

Rounding to the nearest integer, we get

$$r \approx \boxed{8\%}.$$
